<description>
Paint teal bridges through the shortest empty gaps needed to connect each color's solid rectangles.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color and every foreground object is a solid axis-aligned rectangle.
- Rectangles of the same color may face each other horizontally or vertically across empty background.
- Teal is absent from the input and is reserved for the added bridge pixels.

Rule
- Preserve the input and process each foreground color independently.
- Candidate bridges join same-color rectangles whose row or column spans overlap by at least three cells and whose intervening gap is all background.
- Paint the selected gap teal, using the shared span eroded by one pixel on both sides.

Key insight
- The selected bridges are the shortest facing gaps that connect each same-color rectangle group; longer gaps that would only create a cycle are left blank.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "solid same-color rectangular objects s",
  "dst": "empty horizontal or vertical gap d between facing same-color rectangles",
  "match_cond": "same color, overlapping perpendicular span, and all-bg gap; selected gaps connect each color group by shortest gap length",
  "transform": "paint d teal using the shared span eroded by one pixel; keep all input pixels unchanged",
  "multi_step": "process candidate gaps by increasing gap length; skip a gap once its two same-color rectangle groups are already connected"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 25-30 rows x 29-30 cols, background 0 [observed]
  foreground_colors: 2-3 distinct colors, none is teal (8)
  rectangles:
    per_color: 2-6 solid axis-aligned rectangles
    dimensions: 3-9 height x 3-9 width
    total_per_grid: 5-11
    occupancy: 18-29% of grid cells [observed]
  candidate_bridges:
    condition: two same-color rects whose row or column spans overlap by >=3 cells, separated by an all-bg gap of >=1 cell
    per_color_group: enough candidates to form a spanning tree over all rects of that color
  bridge_selection:
    algorithm: minimum spanning tree by gap length (Kruskal); among equal-length candidates, all are used if acyclic
    painted_region: shared span eroded by 1 cell on each side, gap filled with teal (8)
    total_bridges: sum of (n_rects - 1) across all color groups; 0-1 redundant candidates skipped per group
  output: input preserved; teal bridges added in gaps

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (place rects with valid bridging structure, then erase bridges to get input)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size ~25-30 x 29-30, choose 2-3 fg colors (excluding 8).
    2. For each color, pick n_rects (2-6). Build a spanning tree topology over n_rects nodes.
    3. For each tree edge, decide orientation (H or V) and gap length (1-10).
    4. Place rectangles on the grid so each tree-edge pair has the required overlap (>=3) and a clear bg gap of the chosen length. Start from one rect per color group, then place connected rects relative to it. Reject if any rect overlaps another or goes out of bounds.
    5. Optionally add 0-1 extra candidate bridges per color group (cycle edges) with gap length strictly longer than the longest tree edge for that group, to test MST skip logic.
    6. Verify all gap regions are all-bg and no rect of any color overlaps another.
    7. The output is the grid with teal bridges painted; the input is the grid without them.
```
</generation_spec>
